Jahshaka patch 0051 — a manually reserved texture pool is Resident NEXT, too.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this. It touches `OgreMain/src/OgreTextureGpuManager.cpp`, which patch 0056 also
touches (the overlap reset recipe applies to a tree that carries one of them).

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325; audit
SPECS/audits/ENGINE_WORKAROUNDS_TO_PATCHES_2026-09-15.md finding F12).
`TextureGpuManager::reservePoolId` creates the pool master with
`TextureFlags::PoolOwner` only, then calls `_transitionTo( Resident )` +
`notifyDataIsReady()`. `TextureGpu::_transitionTo` assigns
`mNextResidencyStatus = mResidencyStatus` ONLY for a ManualTexture, so the
master is left reading Resident with NEXT = OnStorage — a state that says "this
texture is on its way out to storage". The next `scheduleTransitionTo( Resident )`
on it, which happens as soon as anything binds the pool as a shader texture,
therefore queues a FILE LOAD for a texture that has no file, and the streaming
worker memcpy's from a null mip pointer inside
`TextureGpuManager::processQueuedImage` — a crash, not a message, in a
RelWithDebInfo Ogre where the asserts are compiled out.

The engine carried the one line from outside, right after its own
`reservePoolId` call for the decal atlas masters ("One line, no patch" —
`irisgl/engine/src/OgreDecals.cpp`), which is exactly the shape the rule
forbids: every caller of `reservePoolId` needs it, the next one will not know,
and the state it repairs is not reachable through any public API of the
manager. The nine engine lines are deleted with this patch.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and `git apply
--reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree;
`--engine-selftest` byte-identical (`b55e2d5d…`). The behavioural gate is the
decal suite (`decals.engine`) plus test_engine — a
pool master that never loses residency renders exactly as before, which is the
point: the defect only fires on a transition that should never have been
queued.

--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreTextureGpuManager.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreTextureGpuManager.cpp
@@ -362,6 +362,16 @@
 
         mTexturePool.push_back( newPool );
 
+        // The pool master is RESIDENT from here on and it has no file to load, so
+        // getNextResidencyStatus() must say so too. _transitionTo() only keeps the
+        // two in step for a ManualTexture (TextureGpu::_transitionTo's
+        // isManualTexture() tail), and a pool owner carries TextureFlags::PoolOwner
+        // alone — so without this the master read Resident with next = OnStorage, and
+        // the next scheduleTransitionTo( Resident ) on it (which happens as soon as
+        // something binds the pool as a shader texture) queued a FILE LOAD for a
+        // texture that has no file: the streaming worker then memcpy's from a null
+        // mip pointer in processQueuedImage.
+        newPool.masterTexture->_setNextResidencyStatus( GpuResidency::Resident );
         newPool.masterTexture->_transitionTo( GpuResidency::Resident, 0 );
         newPool.masterTexture->notifyDataIsReady();
 
